FIXME:
1. At present, in each icnt_chLet cycle (see gpu-sim.cc “if(clock_mask & ICNT_chLet)”), each chiplet only pops one mem-fetch, so if we change the inter-chiplet bandwidth not by changing the frequency of icnt_chLet but by input_speedup in Booksim, then icnt_pop_chLet() will become a bottleneck and invalidate the change of input_speedup. 
2. GPPUSim version 4 calls force_l2_tag_update() when doing memcpy (See l2cache.cc memory_partition_unit::handle_memcpy_to_gpu()). Comment it out because we cannot know the sub_partition (= LLC slice) at the memcpy moment in SM-side LLC. (Not sure about the performance impact, but for now we may just comment out force_l2_tag_update() no matter if it's memory-side or SM-side for testing and comparison.)
